---
import SectionHeader from "./SectionHeader.astro";
import ComponentShowcase from "./ComponentShowcase.vue";
---

<section id="components">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHeader num="06" title="Components" sub="A small fixed set of atomic modules, kept only where they solve a concrete UI problem." />

    <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-xl border border-hub-ycp/30 bg-hub-ycp/5 p-6">
      <h4 class="text-[16px] font-semibold mb-2">Powered by Nuxt UI</h4>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground-secondary">
        Mizu now extends Nuxt UI, providing a curated design token layer and theme on top of its robust component library. For common UI primitives — buttons, inputs, dialogs, cards, badges, and more — use Nuxt UI components directly (e.g. <code class="text-xs bg-surface-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;UButton&gt;</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-surface-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;UCard&gt;</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-surface-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;UDialog&gt;</code>) with Mizu's theme applied automatically. The components shown below are Mizu-specific additions that solve unique design problems not covered by Nuxt UI.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ComponentShowcase client:only="vue" />
  </div>
</section>
